I go for a walk across a large square in the city.
Here there is a large flea market every Sunday.
The sun is shining, and many people are walking around between the tables.
I stop by a small table with many different things.
Behind the table stands a friendly vendor.
Suddenly I see two blue ceramic plates.
I pick them up and look closely at them.
"How much do these plates cost?" I ask the vendor.
The vendor smiles at me.
"They cost only forty kroner," he replies.
That is a really good price.
I bought a small table for my kitchen a month ago.
These plates will fit perfectly with this table.
"I would very much like to buy them," I say.
I give the vendor forty kroner and carefully put the plates in my bag.
It is always nice to find something special on a quiet Sunday.
